  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a binary string SSS of size NNN. A string is called **good** if\n\n\nThe first character of the string is 000.\nThe last character of the string is 111.\nCount the number of sub-strings in SSS which are **good**. Since the answer might be a large number, print it modulo 109+710^{9} + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of testcases. Then the testcases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line of each test case contains a single string SSS.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, print the count of good sub-strings modulo 109+710^{9} + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "Each character of string SSS is either 000 or 111.",
      "Subtasks",
      "30 points : 1≤N≤1001 \\leq N \\leq 1001≤N≤100",
      "70 points : 1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
